import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.Asymptotics.KhatE1Core.XtruncRemBoundNotes

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 10000

/-!
# The explicit remainders `XR4`, `XW`: tree-shaped cluster **defs**

`Bracket24XtruncRing` (`Xtrunc2_decomp`) writes the remainder of the truncated `d = 24` bracket as

  `(Ept z)^4 · XR4 ℓ τ z + (Ept z)^6 · XW ℓ τ z`,

with `XR4` (29 monomials) and `XW` (253 monomials) *explicit* sums of monomials in the atoms.
Here they are bounded in the `BoundQ` calculus:

  `‖XR4 ℓ τ z‖ ≤ C (scale τ)^N (1+t)^M`  and  `‖XW ℓ τ z‖ ≤ C ‖q(τ)‖⁻¹ (scale τ)^N (1+t)^M`.

## Why this file is shaped the way it is

Both definitions are written as *balanced binary trees* of `+` (not flat sums), so the same
expressions are also *definitionally* decomposable along that tree: replacing a maximal subtree of
at most `16` leaves by a fresh `def` whose body is that very subtree changes nothing up to
`rfl`.  Hence this file

* copies the two definitions verbatim as `XR4t_all`, `XWt_all` (so the module is self-contained and
  does not have to wait for `Bracket24XtruncRing` to compile: once it does, the two glue lemmas
  `XR4 ℓ τ z = XR4t_all ℓ τ z` and `XW ℓ τ z = XWt_all ℓ τ z` are `rfl`, since the bodies are
  literally the same text);
* cuts each tree into maximal subtrees of `≤ 16` leaves, one `def` per cluster
  (`XR4t_c1 …`, `XWt_c1 …`), with the *tree-shape* decomposition `…_all = <tree of clusters>`
  proved by `rfl` (`XWt_all_eq`, `XR4t_all_eq`) — no `ring`, no re-association, no giant goal;
* proves one `BoundQ` bound *per cluster* (each a goal with at most 16 monomials — cheap), and
  assembles them by the `BoundQ` calculus (`add` takes the `min` of the exponents).

The one genuine weight point is the pair of `j(τ)²`-monomials of `XW`
(`(7/4)π⁻¹Ept·E₄²ψ₄j²` and `-(7/4)π⁻¹Ept·E₄E₆ψ₂j²`): they sit in a *single* cluster, whose bound is
proved by grouping them into the near-identity `(7/4)π⁻¹Ept·j²(ψ₄E₈ − ψ₂E₁₀)`
(`BoundQ_theta24_group`, `XtruncRemBoundNotes`), which is `O(‖q(τ)‖⁻¹(scale τ)^N)` exactly like
the other monomials.
-/

